<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 58 0 R/Pg 12 0 R/A[359 0 R 0]/K[17]>>
endobj

107 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 59 0 R/T(      Why can it happen? )/E(      Why can it happen? )/Pg 13 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

108 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(Most of the time, premature births happen spontaneously \(naturally\) and doctors will not know why.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

109 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(Sometimes, a premature birth is planned because it's safer for mum/parent and/or the baby. This could be because either have a health condition, such as severe pre-eclampsia, that means it is safer not to continue the pregnancy.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[2 271 0 R 4]>>
endobj

110 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Span/K[3]/Pg 13 0 R/P 271 0 R>>
endobj

111 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(There are some things that increase the risk of going into labour early, so some people may be told that they have a higher risk of giving birth early. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[5 272 0 R 7]>>
endobj

112 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Span/K[6]/Pg 13 0 R/P 272 0 R>>
endobj

113 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 59 0 R/T(Previous premature birth)/E(Previous premature birth)/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

114 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(If you\220ve given birth early before, you are more likely to give birth early again. The more premature deliveries you have had, and the earlier your babies were born, the higher this risk becomes, but there is no guanerentee.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

115 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 59 0 R/T(Previous late miscarriage)/E(Previous late miscarriage)/Pg 13 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

116 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(The causes of late miscarriage and premature birth can be the same. If you had a late miscarriage before then you may have a higher chance of having a late miscarriage or a premature birth in a next pregnancy. It doesn't mean that it will happen though. The more the doctors know about the reasons for the previous experience, the more they will be able to make sure it doesn't happen again.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[11 273 0 R 13]>>
endobj

117 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Span/K[12]/Pg 13 0 R/P 273 0 R>>
endobj

118 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 59 0 R/T(Low PAPP-A levels )/E(Low PAPP-A levels )/Pg 13 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

119 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(Pregnancy Associated Plasma Protein-A \(PAPP-A\) is a hormone that is made by the placenta in pregnancy. It is measured as part of the antenatal screening tests you are offered during pregnancy.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

120 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(Low levels of PAPP-A may mean that the placenta \(the organ that helps the baby grow and develop\) may not work as well. There may be an increased chance of premature birth or pre-eclampsia. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[16 274 0 R 18]>>
endobj

121 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Span/K[17]/Pg 13 0 R/P 274 0 R>>
endobj

122 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(If you are diagnosed with low levels of PAPP-A you\220ll likely be offered extra scans to monitor your baby\220s growth. It\220s also important to get to know your baby\220s movements and contact your midwife or maternity unit immediately if you think your baby\220s movements have slowed down, stopped or changed.  )/Pg 13 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

123 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 59 0 R/T(Placenta praevia)/E(Placenta praevia)/Pg 13 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

124 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(Sometimes the placenta attaches low down in the uterus and may cover part of or all of the cervix. In most cases, the placenta moves upwards and out of the way with the uterus as it growns, and as pregnancy continues, but sometimes it doesn\220t.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

125 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 59 0 R/E(This condition is known as low-lying placenta if the placenta is less than 20 mm from the cervix or as placenta praevia if the placenta covers the cervix. If you have placenta praevia, you are at a higher risk of giving birth early. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

126 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 59 0 R/Pg 13 0 R/A[360 0 R 0]/K[23]>>
endobj

